# wiring guide, solar tracker (team 20)

follow top to bottom. each part ends with a quick check so you know it works before moving on.
every pin below matches `include/config.h` as it is now. if you use a different pin, write it in the
"your pin" column and change that line in config.h.

## 0. rules (read once)

1. all grounds are tied together: battery -, buck -, motor driver gnd, esp32 gnd, every sensor gnd.
2. esp32 pins are 3.3 v. nothing over 3.3 v ever goes into an esp32 pin.
3. 12 v only goes to: fuse, ina260 vin+ / vin-, motor driver P+, buck input. never near the esp32 header.
4. set the buck to 5.0 v on its display BEFORE connecting it to anything.
5. wire with the battery disconnected. connect the battery last.
6. while the esp32 is plugged into the laptop by usb, do NOT also connect the buck's 5 v to it. usb or buck, never both.

## 1. pin map at a glance

| esp32 pin | goes to | config.h name | your pin |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 3V3 | logic power for encoders, ina260, motor driver VCC, light circuit, anemometer pull-up | - | 3V3 |
| 5V | gps vcc (and buck 5 v out when not on usb) | - | 5V |
| GND | common ground | - | GND |
| IO21 | tilt as5600 SDA + ina260 SDA | PIN_I2C_TILT_SDA | ____ |
| IO22 | tilt as5600 SCL + ina260 SCL | PIN_I2C_TILT_SCL | ____ |
| IO18 | azimuth as5600 SDA | PIN_I2C_AZ_SDA | ____ |
| IO19 | azimuth as5600 SCL | PIN_I2C_AZ_SCL | ____ |
| IO4 | gps TX | PIN_GPS_RX | ____ |
| IO23 | gps RX | PIN_GPS_TX | ____ |
| IO26 | motor driver INA1 (tilt) | PIN_TILT_MOTOR_A | ____ |
| IO33 | motor driver INB1 (tilt) | PIN_TILT_MOTOR_B | ____ |
| IO25 | motor driver PWM1 (tilt) | PIN_TILT_MOTOR_C | ____ |
| IO13 | motor driver INA2 (azimuth) | PIN_AZ_MOTOR_A | ____ |
| IO14 | motor driver INB2 (azimuth) | PIN_AZ_MOTOR_B | ____ |
| IO27 | motor driver PWM2 (azimuth) | PIN_AZ_MOTOR_C | ____ |
| IO34 | light circuit output | PIN_PHOTODIODE_ADC | ____ |
| IO32 | tps22917 ON (light circuit power switch) | PIN_SENSOR_LOAD_SW | ____ |
| IO35 | anemometer signal | PIN_ANEMOMETER | ____ |

if you move a pin: never use 6-11 (flash). avoid 0, 2, 5, 12, 15 for outputs. 34-39 are input only
(fine for light and anemometer, not for motors). the light circuit must stay on 32-39.

## 2. power (12 v side)

```
battery +  -> inline fuse -> splits into two:
                 a) ina260 Vin+  -> ina260 Vin-  -> motor driver P+
                 b) buck input +
battery -  -> motor driver P-, buck input -, buck output -, esp32 GND (all one ground)
buck output + (set to 5.0 v) -> esp32 5V   (only when the esp32 is NOT on usb)
```

- fuse: start with 10 a. after `stroke` prints the peak current, pick about 1.5x that.
- motor driver (dfr0601) power input is 6.5-37 v on P+ / P-. the battery is 12 v, fine.
- buck (dfr0379): input 4-40 v, output adjustable. touch button on it switches the display between in and out voltage. set out to 5.0 v first.

check: battery connected, buck display reads 5.0 v out, motor driver STATE led on and steady (fast blink = over-voltage, slow blink = under-voltage).

## 3. motor driver (dfr0601) + actuators

logic side:
- VCC -> esp32 3V3
- GND -> esp32 GND
- INA1 -> IO26, INB1 -> IO33, PWM1 -> IO25 (tilt)
- INA2 -> IO13, INB2 -> IO14, PWM2 -> IO27 (azimuth)
- 10k resistor from IO25 to GND, and 10k from IO27 to GND (keeps motors off while the esp32 boots)

motor side:
- tilt actuator (lower one, base on the mast): its two wires -> M1_A and M1_B
- azimuth actuator (upper one, base on the hanging strut): its two wires -> M2_A and M2_B
- wire order does not matter yet. if "extend" retracts, swap the two wires or set `TILT_MOTOR_INVERT` / `AZ_MOTOR_INVERT = true`.

check (after section 9 upload): `jog t ext 500` moves the tilt actuator a little, `jog a ext 500` moves azimuth.

## 4. ina260 (current sensor, tilt i2c bus)

- VCC -> 3V3, GND -> GND
- SDA -> IO21, SCL -> IO22 (shared with the tilt encoder, that is fine, different address)
- Vin+ / Vin- are in the 12 v line to the motor driver (section 2). Vin+ toward the battery, Vin- toward the driver.
- leave A0 / A1 pads alone (address 0x40)

check: `i2cscan` shows 0x40 on Wire (tilt).

## 5. tilt encoder (as5600, tilt i2c bus)

- VIN -> 3V3, GND -> GND, SDA -> IO21, SCL -> IO22 (stemma qt cable or jumpers)
- leave DIR as it ships (tied to gnd), direction is set in software
- mount: magnet on the end of the tilt shoulder bolt (turns with the crossbar), chip on the mast plate facing it, 0.5-3 mm gap, centered

check: `i2cscan` shows 0x36 on Wire. `raw` says "magnet detected", no TOO WEAK / TOO STRONG, raw changes when the crossbar is tilted by hand.

## 6. azimuth encoder (as5600, its own i2c bus)

- VIN -> 3V3, GND -> GND, SDA -> IO18, SCL -> IO19
- it needs its own bus because every as5600 has the same address (0x36)
- mount: magnet on the azimuth shaft end, chip on the pillow block / crossbar side. NOT on anything fixed to the ground, or every tilt move looks like an azimuth move.
- route both encoder cables away from the actuator power wires, keep them as short as you can

check: `i2cscan` shows 0x36 on Wire1 (azimuth). `raw` shows the azimuth raw changing when the panel is rolled by hand.

## 7. gps (neo-6m)

- VCC -> 5V (worked in test 2.3), GND -> GND
- gps TX -> IO4, gps RX -> IO23   (this replaces the IO26 / IO27 wiring from test 2.3, IO26 is now a motor pin)
- antenna needs open sky, not inside a metal box

check: `status` shows gps chars climbing right away, and "synced" plus satellites once it is outside. `sun` then prints the sun position.

## 8. light circuit and anemometer

light circuit (eyuel's photodiode + amp):
- tps22917 ON -> IO32, tps22917 VIN -> 3V3, tps22917 VOUT -> powers the amp
- amp output -> IO34. must never go above 3.3 v, check with a meter in full sun before connecting.
- ground shared

anemometer:
- if it is a 2-wire switch type: one wire -> IO35, other wire -> GND, plus a 10k resistor from IO35 to 3V3 (IO35 has no internal pull-up)
- if it has 3 wires or puts out a voltage: stop and check the datasheet first, IO35 cannot take over 3.3 v

check: `light` prints millivolts that go up with a flashlight and down when covered.

## 9. first upload and checks, in this order

1. esp32 on usb only (buck 5 v disconnected from it), battery connected for the motors.
2. upload, open serial monitor at 115200.
3. boot shows `sun table: 2026 ... crc ok, in use` and a list of missing config values. that list is expected.
4. `i2cscan` -> 0x36 + 0x40 on Wire, 0x36 on Wire1
5. `raw` -> both magnets detected
6. `jog t ext 500`, `jog a ext 500` -> each actuator moves a little
7. `light` -> millivolts react to light
8. `status` -> gps chars climbing

## 10. values to fill in (config.h), after wiring works

| value | how to get it | write it here |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TILT_ACT_RETRACTED_IN | tape measure, pin center to pin center, fully retracted | ____ |
| TILT_ACT_EXTENDED_IN | same, fully extended (should be retracted + about 12.81) | ____ |
| AZ_ACT_RETRACTED_IN | same for the azimuth actuator | ____ |
| AZ_ACT_EXTENDED_IN | same | ____ |
| TILT_ACT_SPEED_IN_S | `stroke t ext` prints it | ____ |
| AZ_ACT_SPEED_IN_S | `stroke a ext` prints it | ____ |
| MOVE_POWER_W | `stroke` prints it | ____ |
| OVERCURRENT_A | `stroke` prints it | ____ |
| TILT_EXTEND_SIGN | `jog t ext 500`: panel tipped south = +1, north = -1 | ____ |
| AZ_EXTEND_SIGN | `jog a ext 500`: panel tipped east = +1, west = -1 | ____ |
| TILT_ENC_DIR | `jog t ext 500`: raw went up while panel moved south = +1, else -1 | ____ |
| AZ_ENC_DIR | `jog a ext 500`: raw went up while panel moved east = +1, else -1 | ____ |
| TILT_ENC_STOW_RAW | `calibrate` prints it (do this after everything above, then upload again) | ____ |
| AZ_ENC_STOW_RAW | `calibrate` prints it | ____ |
| LIGHT_LUX_PER_MV | phone lux meter app next to the sensor: lux / the mV from `light` | ____ |
| LIGHT_MIN_LUX | team pick, ~20000 to start (full sun ~100000, overcast ~1000-10000) | ____ |

after these are in and uploaded, the boot list should show no `[blocks motion]` lines. then:
`sun` (no motion) -> `goto t 10` -> `goto a 5` -> `stow` -> `cycle` -> `resume`.

## 11. if something is off

| symptom | likely cause |
| --- | --- |
| `i2cscan` finds nothing | sda / scl swapped, no 3V3 or gnd to the board, wrong pins in config.h |
| `raw` says magnet MISSING or TOO WEAK | magnet too far (keep 0.5-3 mm) or off center |
| `raw` says TOO STRONG | magnet too close |
| raw jumps around while a motor runs | encoder cable next to actuator wires, reroute, keep it short |
| actuator does not move on `jog` | motor driver VCC / gnd missing, battery not connected, STATE led blinking (check voltage) |
| jog extend actually retracts | swap the two actuator wires, or set *_MOTOR_INVERT = true |
| motor twitches at power-up | 10k pull-downs on IO25 / IO27 missing |
| gps chars stay at 0 | gps tx / rx swapped (gps TX must go to IO4) |
| gps chars climb but no sync | indoors, take it outside |
| `light` reads 0 or 3300 mV constantly | tps22917 ON not wired to IO32, or amp output stuck / over range |
| esp32 resets when a motor starts | weak 5 v or missing common ground, check the buck and grounds |
